WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.403
- I wanna ask you about
something more serious

00:00:01.403 --> 00:00:03.720
because you went to a
Ukraine recently, right?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.730
And this is, it's really
important to a lot of people,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.530
but why did you feel
like you wanted to go?

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.530
- I have a lot of friends who
are Ukrainian and, you know

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.250
I was talking to someone,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.040
when everything first started
to happen and I, you know,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.290
said how sad I was and asked, said,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.700
Please, if there's anything

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.380
that I could ever do to help, let me know.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.330
And then I was reached out to,

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.030
to ask if I would go and visit.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.220
- Yeah.
- And I said, absolutely.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.020
It was a pretty intense thing.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.370
I've never done anything like that before.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.560
I mean, I flew to Warsaw and then drove

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.540
like four and a half
hours to a train station

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.930
and then took a train for
12 hours to get to Kiev and

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.160
- [Kelly] Wow.
- Yeah.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.510
You know, and for the most of the journey

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.460
without a translator and without security,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.320
I mean it was just me and my friend.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.960
And when I got there, I met
so many incredible people.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.480
I went to the children's hospital there.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.905
I mean, my heart's just breaking

00:00:52.905 --> 00:00:54.960
with everything that
they're struggling with.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.340
And I just, I don't understand,
every time I open the news,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.470
I'm just so sad about the things

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.210
that are happening in this world.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.240
The stuff that's happening in Iran.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.700
Just, it's a constant sense of,

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.290
we really need to look out for each other

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.230
and we really need to, for
me I wanna use my platform

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.450
to amplify the voices of those

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.390
that are fighting for freedom, and,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.890
- And you get to tell their stories.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.840
That's what I love about movies too.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.233
It's such a cool vessel
to tell people's stories.

